  "preamble": "A coda rhotic can assimilate completely to a following [p], giving a geminate [pp] (rp > pp). In Middle Indo-Aryan, Sanskrit r assimilated to a following stop, nasal, sibilant or v, so sarpá 'snake' became Pali sappa and arpáyati became appeti. The change is always conditioned by a following p.",
